 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "src/marketentry/* (langgraph-clj StateGraph actor, compiled via
 `operation/build` -> `g/state-graph` -> `g/compile-graph` with
 `interrupt-before #{:request-approval}`): facts.cljc (official
 spec-basis catalog -- Uzņēmumu reģistrs business registration, PIL/
 IUB procurement-law compliance, EIS platform registration, VID VAT
 registration; keeps IUB's legal/regulatory-oversight role and VDAA's
 separate EIS technical-operator role, renamed from VRAA in 2024, as
 two DISTINCT catalog fields), governor.cljc (Market-Entry Compliance
 Governor -- spec-basis HARD check, evidence-incomplete HARD check,
 `:ur-registration-missing` HARD check independently verifying
 `:has-ur-registration?` when `:requires-ur-registration?` is true,
 `:platform-operator-fused` HARD check independently verifying a
 `:jurisdiction/assess` proposal never collapses IUB and VDAA into one
 fused authority -- the FLAGSHIP new check for this vertical, grounded
 in the regulator/operator split verified for EIS (eis.gov.lv) --,
 engagement-fee-mismatch independent recompute, `:vat-unverified` HARD
 check (VID VAT Register), confidence-floor/actuation gate, plus
 double-draft/double-submit guards), store.cljc (MemStore +
 DatomicStore via `io.github.kotoba-lang/langchain-store`
 (`ls/enc`/`ls/dec*`/`ls/read-stream`/`ls/append-blob!`) instead of a
 hand-rolled EDN-blob codec), registry.cljc (pure-function
 filing-draft/filing-submit record construction + fee recompute),
 marketentryllm.cljc (mock MarketEntry Advisor, with an injectable
 `:fuse-platform-operator?` failure mode alongside the shared
 `:no-spec?` one), operation.cljc (intake -> advise -> govern -> decide
 -> [request-approval ->] commit/hold StateGraph, `store/append-ledger!`
 called from both the `:commit` and `:hold` nodes), phase.cljc (0->3
 rollout, `:filing/draft`/`:filing/submit` permanently excluded from
 every phase's `:auto` set). Plus src/statute/facts.cljc (general-law
 compliance catalog, ADR-2607141700 `cloud-itonami-compliance-fact-
 federation` -- orthogonal to marketentry.facts's procurement-only
 scope: Komerclikums/Commercial Law (adopted 13.04.2000, in force since
 01.01.2002), Fizisko personu datu apstrādes likums/Personal Data
 Processing Law (adopted 21.06.2018, in force since 05.07.2018,
 supplements EU Regulation 2016/679 GDPR at the national level), Darba
 likums/Labour Law (adopted 20.06.2001, in force since 01.06.2002) --
 all three independently WebFetch-verified against likumi.lv (both the
 normal document page and its print-friendly metadata view), none
 duplicating or contradicting the IUB/VDAA platform-operator-split fact
 `marketentry.facts` already owns, `lva.komerclikums` explicitly built
 on top of (not re-deriving) `marketentry.facts`'s own Uzņēmumu
 reģistrs citation), schema/statute.edn (DataScript schema) and
 data/datascript-tx.edn (derived tx-data), mirroring the
 cloud-itonami-iso3166-est/-isl/-swe/-nor/-dnk/-fin sibling convention.
 Tests cover the governor contract (including the IUB/VDAA distinction,
 both the clean path and the fused-claim HARD hold), facts, phase,
 registry, store parity (MemStore vs DatomicStore) and ledger
 append-only-ness across both backends, plus this repo's separate
 `culture` domain namespace and the new `statute` catalog (including a
 dedicated test asserting the statute catalog never re-fuses or
 restates the IUB/VDAA split), left untouched. 43 tests / 157
 assertions passing (up from 37 tests / 136 assertions before this
 change -- the 6 new tests / 21 new assertions are all in
 `statute.facts-test`), clj-kondo clean (0 errors, 8 non-fatal
 unused-binding/unused-require warnings, all pre-existing in
 `src/marketentry/*` and unrelated to this change)."}
